  "body": "`test_readme_with_all_quality_signals` asserts `data[\"word_count\"] > 100` and `word_count_category == \"comprehensive\"`, but its fixture README contains only ~51 words, so the test fails against correct scorer behavior. Extend the fixture (or correct the assertion) so the test validates what it intends to.\n\n**Steps to reproduce:** `pytest tests/unit/test_readme_scorer.py -q` — observed: `assert 51 > 100` fails.",
